#N canvas 40 40 1200 800 12;
#X text 20 20 u_root -- the actual root of Cut It. main.pd (on the device) and main-dev.pd (on the Mac) both instantiate this and nothing else \, which is what stops the two entry points drifting., f 58;
#X text 20 110 creation args: none. inlets: none. outlets: none., f 58;
#X text 20 145 THE AUDIO PATH IS WIRES \, ON PURPOSE. The four stages go in the gap below \, right to left \, so the chain stays something you can read off the canvas instead of tracing through send names., f 58;
#X obj 20 300 r~ inL;
#X obj 20 580 throw~ outL;
#X obj 330 300 r~ inR;
#X obj 330 580 throw~ outR;
#X obj 170 360 u_level in-l;
#X obj 480 360 u_level in-r;
#X text 70 440 Phase 3+: e_chop \, e_pitch \, e_trem \, e_verb go in this gap., f 30;
#X text 650 300 L = drums \, R = fx: the SP-404's hard-panned outputs arriving through the TRS Y-cable. adc~ 1 is the tip \, verified -- plan-tests.md item 11., f 34;
#X obj 650 430 g_levels;
#X text 650 470 owns the OLED. Anything wanting to display something sends to disp -- nothing else touches oscOut or screenLine., f 34;
#X text 650 580 The level taps are a SIGNAL fan-out \, which needs no trigger: signal connections all run every block \, so there is no firing order to get wrong. The trigger rule is about messages., f 34;
#X text 20 640 adc~ and dac~ appear NOWHERE in this patch \, and must not. mother.pd owns both -- it publishes the inputs on inL / inR and collects the output from outL / outR \, then applies the volume knob and a limiter. A patch that writes to dac~ silently bypasses both. See plan-conventions.md \, Audio I/O., f 58;
#X connect 3 0 4 0;
#X connect 3 0 7 0;
#X connect 5 0 6 0;
#X connect 5 0 8 0;
